  "id": "COMPOUND:27025 - PROTEIN:5866",
  "verbalization": "Hypocrellol B appears to interact with multiple targets that ultimately lead to a relationship with NCI-H446. The evidence suggests that Hypocrellol B targets P-selectin glycoprotein ligand 1, which is a known target of SGI-1776, and both SGI-1776 and Vatalbinoside C are implicated in targeting NCI-H446. Similarly, Hypocrellol B also targets CDK3/cyclin E, which is a target of Vatalbinoside C and Acronyculatin E, both of which also target NCI-H446. These pathways collectively indicate that Hypocrellol B may exert its effects through multiple molecular mechanisms that ultimately engage NCI-H446. The integration of these targets highlights a potential role for Hypocrellol B in modulating NCI-H446 through diverse signaling pathways, suggesting a complex, multi-target interaction network.",
